{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01SBSBHC3t7ygZuPLcTN9FX5","type":"tool_result","content":"\"\"\"Why the ridge is where it is: the hardness peak as a condition on one graph parameter.\n\nQuestion (`reports/ml_nature_plan_2.md` §2.9, loop0003 item 11). §11 put the\nhardness ridge -- the density at which the nodes to refute `optimum - 1` peak\nat fixed `n` -- at three customers per product when `m = n` and two when\n`m = 2n`; §16 found it at five to six when `m = n / 2`. In which coordinate is\nthat one number? The plan's hypothesis was the MOSP-graph mean degree\n(\"8-9 at both ratios\"). This module (a) derives, for both generators, the\nexpected degree, edge probability, giant-component branching factor and the\nincidence-graph excess of `G(n, m, p)` in `col_mean` coordinates, checks the\nderivations against the measured graphs, (b) locates every series' peak by\nparabolic interpolation between cells with bootstrap intervals, (c) tests\neach candidate parameter for constancy across `m / n`, (d) calibrates every\nhypothesis on the `m = n` ridge and predicts the `m = n / 2`, `m = n / 4`\nand `m = n / 8` ridges from it, and (e) runs the deciding cells the campaign\nlacked: `m = n / 4` at n in {50, 60, 75} and `m = n / 8` at n = 75, where the\ndegree and excess hypotheses are furthest apart.\n\nNothing here is a bound or a solver change; nothing is written to\n`solutions/`. Generated instances are certified with `solve_mosp_exact` into\n`learning/data/ensemble/solutions/` like the rest of the campaign, and their\nrows go to `learning/data/ensemble/results_ratio.csv` (with a manifest), kept\napart from `results.csv` and `results_upward.csv` so §10-§16 regenerate\nunchanged.\n\nUsage:\n    python -m learning.ridge_theory --stage run --workers 16    # the m = n/4 and n/8 cells (~10 min)\n    python -m learning.ridge_theory --stage tables              # reports/ridge_theory_tables.md + figure, ~30 s\n    python -m pytest tests/test_ridge_theory.py -q\n\"\"\"\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport argparse\nimport time\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nimport numpy as np\nimport pandas as pd\n\nfrom learning.ensemble import (ENSEMBLE_DIR, RESULTS_CSV, RESULTS_UPWARD_CSV, Cell, load_results,\n                               run, write_manifest)\nfrom learning.upward import apply_finish, prepare\n\nRESULTS_RATIO_CSV = ENSEMBLE_DIR / \"results_ratio.csv\"\nMANIFEST_RATIO_CSV = ENSEMBLE_DIR / \"manifest_ratio.csv\"\nCLIQUES_CSV = ENSEMBLE_DIR / \"ridge_clique_excess.csv\"\nTABLES = Path(\"reports/ridge_theory_tables.md\")\nFIGURE = Path(\"reports/figures/ridge_theory.png\")\n\nRATIO_N = (50, 60, 75)\nRATIO_D = (3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 8, 9, 10, 12)\nRATIO_P = (0.05, 0.075, 0.1, 0.125, 0.15, 0.2)\nEIGHTH_N = 75\nEIGHTH_D = (4, 6, 8, 10, 12, 14, 16, 18, 20, 24)\nPER_CELL = 50\nSEED = 0\n\n\ndef ratio_cells(sizes=RATIO_N, ds=RATIO_D, ps=RATIO_P) -> list[Cell]:\n    \"\"\"m = n // 4 at each size, fixed d and Bernoulli p; plus m = n // 8 at 75, fixed only.\"\"\"\ndef ratio_cells(sizes=RATIO_N, ds=RATIO_D, ps=RATIO_P) -> list[Cell]:\n    \"\"\"m = n // 4 at each size, fixed d and Bernoulli p; plus m = n // 8 at 75, fixed only.\"\"\"\n    cells: list[Cell] = []\n    for n in sizes:\n        m = n // 4\n        cells += [Cell(\"fixed\", n, m, d) for d in ds if d <= n]\n        cells += [Cell(\"bernoulli\", n, m, p) for p in ps]\n    m8 = EIGHTH_N // 8\n    cells += [Cell(\"fixed\", EIGHTH_N, m8, d) for d in EIGHTH_D if d <= EIGHTH_N]\n    return cells\n\n\ndef run_ratio(workers: int = 16, per_cell: int = PER_CELL, csv: Path = RESULTS_RATIO_CSV) -> pd.DataFrame:\n    cells = ratio_cells()\n    # densest first: the sparse cells are the slow ones at m = n / 4 (they are the ridge)\n    frame = run(cells, per_cell, workers=workers, csv=csv, instance_dir=None, deadline=120.0, solve_budget=600.0)\n    write_manifest(frame, MANIFEST_RATIO_CSV)\n    return frame\n\n\n\nCLIQUE_CAP = 20_000\n\n\ndef clique_excess_of(instance, cap: int = CLIQUE_CAP) -> dict:\n97:def prepare(frame: pd.DataFrame, config: str = \"default\") -> pd.DataFrame:\ninstance_name,bip_cyc_exact,bip_components,core2_cust_frac,core2_prod_frac,core2_edges_n,core2_cyc_n,core2_cyc_per_core_cust,core2_excess,core2_row_mean,core2_components,core32_cust_frac,core32_prod_frac,core32_edges_n,core32_cyc_n,core32_cyc_per_core_cust,core32_excess,core32_row_mean,core32_components,core23_cust_frac,core23_prod_frac,core23_edges_n,core23_cyc_n,core23_cyc_per_core_cust,core23_excess,core23_row_mean,core23_components,core33_cust_frac,core33_prod_frac,core33_edges_n,core33_cyc_n,core33_cyc_per_core_cust,core33_excess,core33_row_mean,core33_components,dom_cust_frac,dom_prod_frac,dom_excess,dom_cyc_per_cust,dom_row_mean\n69:def ridge100_values() -> dict[str, dict]:\n80:def _prefix_job(args) -> dict:\n104:def load_prefix(path: Path = PREFIX_CSV) -> pd.DataFrame:\n110:def _append(row: dict, path: Path) -> None:\n115:def prefix_run(workers: int = 16, deadline: float = 2400.0, wall: float = 4500.0, min_call: float = 300.0,\n170:def campaign_series(config: str, d: float = 3.0, max_n: int = 75) -> pd.DataFrame:\n189:def upward100_series(config: str, d: float = 4.0) -> pd.DataFrame:\n205:def ridge100_series(config: str, prefix_csv: Path = PREFIX_CSV, calls_csv: Path = CALLS_CSV,\n237:def series(config: str, d: float = 3.0, with_100: bool = True) -> pd.DataFrame:\n258:def mean_of(model: str, theta: np.ndarray, n: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:\n273:def rate_of(model: str, theta: np.ndarray, n: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:\n288:def _negloglik(params: np.ndarray, model: str, n: np.ndarray, y: np.ndarray, cens: np.ndarray) -> float:\n298:def _start(model: str, n: np.ndarray, y: np.ndarray, cens: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:\n317:def fit(frame: pd.DataFrame, model: str = \"quadratic\", n_min: int = 10, n_max: int = 100) -> dict:\n353:def _boot_chunk(args) -> list[dict]:\n369:def bootstrap_fit(frame: pd.DataFrame, model: str, n_min: int, n_max: int, resamples: int = 300,\n395:def cell_location(frame: pd.DataFrame, n: int, sigma: float) -> dict:\n422:def recertify_counts(path: Path = RECERTIFY) -> pd.DataFrame:\n430:def corpus100(path: Path = SCALE_NODES) -> pd.DataFrame:\n442:def fix_cost_100(prefix_csv: Path = PREFIX_CSV, calls_csv: Path = CALLS_CSV, price_csv: Path = PRICE_CSV) -> pd.DataFrame:\n488:def hours(log_nodes: float, nodes_per_second: float = NODES_PER_SECOND[0]) -> float:\n496:def readings_table(frame: pd.DataFrame, config: str, d: float, resamples: int = 300,\n547:def compare_with_record(readings: pd.DataFrame, rec: pd.DataFrame, d: float) -> pd.DataFrame:\n560:def fix_ratio_summary(fc: pd.DataFrame) -> dict:\n577:def class_cost_table(readings_by_d: dict[float, pd.DataFrame], fix: dict,\n605:def _md(frame: pd.DataFrame, floatfmt: str = \".3g\") -> str:\n609:def tables(out: Path = TABLES, resamples: int = 300, verbose: bool = True, workers: int = 8) -> dict:\n703:def main() -> None:","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7926e52b-a7c9-488a-920f-3bf6526697d2","uuid":"212c0da5-ffae-4dff-ab96-1fc05d28e2aa","timestamp":"2026-09-28T01:10:39.849Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"\"\"\"Why the ridge is where it is: the hardness peak as a condition on one graph parameter.\n\nQuestion (`reports/ml_nature_plan_2.md` §2.9, loop0003 item 11). §11 put the\nhardness ridge -- the density at which the nodes to refute `optimum - 1` peak\nat fixed `n` -- at three customers per product when `m = n` and two when\n`m = 2n`; §16 found it at five to six when `m = n / 2`. In which coordinate is\nthat one number? The plan's hypothesis was the MOSP-graph mean degree\n(\"8-9 at both ratios\"). This module (a) derives, for both generators, the\nexpected degree, edge probability, giant-component branching factor and the\nincidence-graph excess of `G(n, m, p)` in `col_mean` coordinates, checks the\nderivations against the measured graphs, (b) locates every series' peak by\nparabolic interpolation between cells with bootstrap intervals, (c) tests\neach candidate parameter for constancy across `m / n`, (d) calibrates every\nhypothesis on the `m = n` ridge and predicts the `m = n / 2`, `m = n / 4`\nand `m = n / 8` ridges from it, and (e) runs the deciding cells the campaign\nlacked: `m = n / 4` at n in {50, 60, 75} and `m = n / 8` at n = 75, where the\ndegree and excess hypotheses are furthest apart.\n\nNothing here is a bound or a solver change; nothing is written to\n`solutions/`. Generated instances are certified with `solve_mosp_exact` into\n`learning/data/ensemble/solutions/` like the rest of the campaign, and their\nrows go to `learning/data/ensemble/results_ratio.csv` (with a manifest), kept\napart from `results.csv` and `results_upward.csv` so §10-§16 regenerate\nunchanged.\n\nUsage:\n    python -m learning.ridge_theory --stage run --workers 16    # the m = n/4 and n/8 cells (~10 min)\n    python -m learning.ridge_theory --stage tables              # reports/ridge_theory_tables.md + figure, ~30 s\n    python -m pytest tests/test_ridge_theory.py -q\n\"\"\"\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport argparse\nimport time\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nimport numpy as np\nimport pandas as pd\n\nfrom learning.ensemble import (ENSEMBLE_DIR, RESULTS_CSV, RESULTS_UPWARD_CSV, Cell, load_results,\n                               run, write_manifest)\nfrom learning.upward import apply_finish, prepare\n\nRESULTS_RATIO_CSV = ENSEMBLE_DIR / \"results_ratio.csv\"\nMANIFEST_RATIO_CSV = ENSEMBLE_DIR / \"manifest_ratio.csv\"\nCLIQUES_CSV = ENSEMBLE_DIR / \"ridge_clique_excess.csv\"\nTABLES = Path(\"reports/ridge_theory_tables.md\")\nFIGURE = Path(\"reports/figures/ridge_theory.png\")\n\nRATIO_N = (50, 60, 75)\nRATIO_D = (3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 8, 9, 10, 12)\nRATIO_P = (0.05, 0.075, 0.1, 0.125, 0.15, 0.2)\nEIGHTH_N = 75\nEIGHTH_D = (4, 6, 8, 10, 12, 14, 16, 18, 20, 24)\nPER_CELL = 50\nSEED = 0\n\n\ndef ratio_cells(sizes=RATIO_N, ds=RATIO_D, ps=RATIO_P) -> list[Cell]:\n    \"\"\"m = n // 4 at each size, fixed d and Bernoulli p; plus m = n // 8 at 75, fixed only.\"\"\"\ndef ratio_cells(sizes=RATIO_N, ds=RATIO_D, ps=RATIO_P) -> list[Cell]:\n    \"\"\"m = n // 4 at each size, fixed d and Bernoulli p; plus m = n // 8 at 75, fixed only.\"\"\"\n    cells: list[Cell] = []\n    for n in sizes:\n        m = n // 4\n        cells += [Cell(\"fixed\", n, m, d) for d in ds if d <= n]\n        cells += [Cell(\"bernoulli\", n, m, p) for p in ps]\n    m8 = EIGHTH_N // 8\n    cells += [Cell(\"fixed\", EIGHTH_N, m8, d) for d in EIGHTH_D if d <= EIGHTH_N]\n    return cells\n\n\ndef run_ratio(workers: int = 16, per_cell: int = PER_CELL, csv: Path = RESULTS_RATIO_CSV) -> pd.DataFrame:\n    cells = ratio_cells()\n    # densest first: the sparse cells are the slow ones at m = n / 4 (they are the ridge)\n    frame = run(cells, per_cell, workers=workers, csv=csv, instance_dir=None, deadline=120.0, solve_budget=600.0)\n    write_manifest(frame, MANIFEST_RATIO_CSV)\n    return frame\n\n\n\nCLIQUE_CAP = 20_000\n\n\ndef clique_excess_of(instance, cap: int = CLIQUE_CAP) -> dict:\n97:def prepare(frame: pd.DataFrame, config: str = \"default\") -> pd.DataFrame:\ninstance_name,bip_cyc_exact,bip_components,core2_cust_frac,core2_prod_frac,core2_edges_n,core2_cyc_n,core2_cyc_per_core_cust,core2_excess,core2_row_mean,core2_components,core32_cust_frac,core32_prod_frac,core32_edges_n,core32_cyc_n,core32_cyc_per_core_cust,core32_excess,core32_row_mean,core32_components,core23_cust_frac,core23_prod_frac,core23_edges_n,core23_cyc_n,core23_cyc_per_core_cust,core23_excess,core23_row_mean,core23_components,core33_cust_frac,core33_prod_frac,core33_edges_n,core33_cyc_n,core33_cyc_per_core_cust,core33_excess,core33_row_mean,core33_components,dom_cust_frac,dom_prod_frac,dom_excess,dom_cyc_per_cust,dom_row_mean\n69:def ridge100_values() -> dict[str, dict]:\n80:def _prefix_job(args) -> dict:\n104:def load_prefix(path: Path = PREFIX_CSV) -> pd.DataFrame:\n110:def _append(row: dict, path: Path) -> None:\n115:def prefix_run(workers: int = 16, deadline: float = 2400.0, wall: float = 4500.0, min_call: float = 300.0,\n170:def campaign_series(config: str, d: float = 3.0, max_n: int = 75) -> pd.DataFrame:\n189:def upward100_series(config: str, d: float = 4.0) -> pd.DataFrame:\n205:def ridge100_series(config: str, prefix_csv: Path = PREFIX_CSV, calls_csv: Path = CALLS_CSV,\n237:def series(config: str, d: float = 3.0, with_100: bool = True) -> pd.DataFrame:\n258:def mean_of(model: str, theta: np.ndarray, n: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:\n273:def rate_of(model: str, theta: np.ndarray, n: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:\n288:def _negloglik(params: np.ndarray, model: str, n: np.ndarray, y: np.ndarray, cens: np.ndarray) -> float:\n298:def _start(model: str, n: np.ndarray, y: np.ndarray, cens: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:\n317:def fit(frame: pd.DataFrame, model: str = \"quadratic\", n_min: int = 10, n_max: int = 100) -> dict:\n353:def _boot_chunk(args) -> list[dict]:\n369:def bootstrap_fit(frame: pd.DataFrame, model: str, n_min: int, n_max: int, resamples: int = 300,\n395:def cell_location(frame: pd.DataFrame, n: int, sigma: float) -> dict:\n422:def recertify_counts(path: Path = RECERTIFY) -> pd.DataFrame:\n430:def corpus100(path: Path = SCALE_NODES) -> pd.DataFrame:\n442:def fix_cost_100(prefix_csv: Path = PREFIX_CSV, calls_csv: Path = CALLS_CSV, price_csv: Path = PRICE_CSV) -> pd.DataFrame:\n488:def hours(log_nodes: float, nodes_per_second: float = NODES_PER_SECOND[0]) -> float:\n496:def readings_table(frame: pd.DataFrame, config: str, d: float, resamples: int = 300,\n547:def compare_with_record(readings: pd.DataFrame, rec: pd.DataFrame, d: float) -> pd.DataFrame:\n560:def fix_ratio_summary(fc: pd.DataFrame) -> dict:\n577:def class_cost_table(readings_by_d: dict[float, pd.DataFrame], fix: dict,\n605:def _md(frame: pd.DataFrame, floatfmt: str = \".3g\") -> str:\n609:def tables(out: Path = TABLES, resamples: int = 300, verbose: bool = True, workers: int = 8) -> dict:\n703:def main() -> None:","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false}}
