.07 | 6.93 |\n\n\"\"\"\ns = s[:start] + table + s[end:]\ns = s.replace(\"Leave-series-out 0.20 decades, leave-`n`-out 0.21, and it predicts the two\\ncertified `n / 4` ridges at 100 to +0.16 and +0.21 from the `n ≤ 75` fit.\",\n              \"Leave-series-out 0.21 decades, leave-`n`-out 0.22, and it predicts the two\\ncertified `n / 4` ridges at 100 to +0.16 and +0.21 from the `n ≤ 75` fit\\n(the `n / 2` ridges are another matter: (g)).\")\ns = s.replace(\"makes a linear law work at all (0.30 leave-series-out against 0.54 for the\\nnominal ratio; the quadratic 0.18).\",\n              \"makes a linear law work at all (0.26 leave-series-out against 0.43 for the\\nnominal ratio; the quadratic 0.19).\")\ns = s.replace(\"(pooled `r_eff` linear 0.18 / 0.19 / 0.27; fixed log-clique\\n0.125)\", \"(pooled `r_eff` linear 0.16 / 0.19 / 0.19 in-sample / by series / by `n`;\\nfixed log-clique 0.126)\")\n\n# --- (d) numbers\ns = s.replace(\"\"\"it changes the leave-series-out RMSE by −0.013 to +0.069 decades depending on\nthe base and by +0.004 to −0.056 under `csearch`; the excess-only laws are\noff by a decade.\"\"\", \"\"\"it changes the leave-series-out RMSE by −0.03 to +0.07 decades depending on\nthe base (−0.06 to +0.01 under `csearch`); the excess-only laws are off by a\ndecade.\"\"\")\n\n# --- (g) rewrite\ngstart = s.index(\"### (g) At 100 the law holds\")\ngend = s.index(\"**Finding, in one paragraph.**\")\ng = \"\"\"### (g) At 100 the law holds where the ridge is cheap, and the departure grows with m / n\n\nThe `n ≤ 75` fits put the fixed `m = n` ridge at 100 at 8.4–9.0 decades under\nevery law with `n` in it (`default`); §35's censored-normal location of that\ncell is 10.27 [9.97, 10.68] — every law is 1.3–1.9 decades low, which is the\n75 → 100 rise §35 measured, restated. The two new ratios at 100 sit between:\nthe `n / 4` ridges (certified 5.13 fixed, 5.07 Bernoulli; `col_mean` 10.4\nand 8.4, excess 2.34 and 1.85) are predicted to +0.10 to +0.24, *on* the\nline; t