{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","id":"msg_011CfV4g9pjpMERHDEcE33sV","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Item 10 is done. Nothing is left pending: no background processes of mine are running, `solutions/` is untouched, three items remain unchecked in `iterations.md`, so no `LOOP_COMPLETE` line.\n\n**What the item asked and what it found.** The ridge's height is not a function of the ridge coordinate. The excess at the peak is 2 ± 0.5 in every series and explains none of a height that spans four decades at fixed n. The height is set by n and by the number of products that carry an edge, through one three-parameter law for both generators:\n\n```\nlog10 nodes at the ridge ≈ −0.10 + n · (0.089 + 0.058 · log10(m_eff / n))\n```\n\nwith `m_eff` the products having two or more customers. Held out by series 0.21 decades, by n 0.22, and it predicts the two certified `n/4` ridges at 100 customers to +0.2 from the `n ≤ 75` fit. Adding the excess changes held-out error by −0.03 to +0.07 decades with opposite signs in the two generators. So the deliverable is the second alternative the item allowed, with a formula attached: height needs `m` separately, in the form `n · log(m_eff / n)`.\n\n**Two things the new cells settled.**\n- **§25's \"1–1.5 decades per doubling of m\" saturates for the Bernoulli generator** (0.1–0.25 decades by `m = 8n`) because at the excess-2.4 ridge the edge-carrying products saturate near `2n`; per doubling of `m_eff` the increments are flat at about `0.017 n`, which is what the fixed generator shows directly.\n- **The 75 → 100 rise §35 found on the `m = n` ridge is real and grows with `m / n`.** Two cheap certified cells at 100 were added: the `n/4` ridges land on the `n ≤ 75` law, the `n/2` ridges sit 0.6–1.1 decades above it, and the `m = n` location sits 1.3–1.9 above. Rates per customer over 75 → 100 against 60 → 75: 0.04 → 0.055, 0.07 → 0.10, 0.095 → 0.14.\n\nAlso: with each series' height removed, the whole surface at 50–75 collapses in the excess to r² 0.86–0.94 and not at all in `col_mean`; and the finer Bernoulli `2n` grid lifted §25's peaks by up to half a decade.\n\n**Artifacts.** `learning/ridge_height.py`, `tests/test_ridge_height.py` (10 tests), `reports/ml_nature.md` §37, `reports/ridge_height_tables.md`, and under `learning/data/ensemble/` the results, manifest, effective-product table, three run logs and 3,330 witnesses (18 MB added; the directory is 112 MB apparent). 3,380 new instances in 82 cells, 3,378 certified under both configurations. Full suite after the last edit: 1,200 passed, 2 skipped, 1 xfailed. PROGRESS.md has the iteration entry and reads 10/13 solved; the item is ticked in `iterations.md`.\n\n**Caveats recorded in the report.** The fixed `m = 2n` peaks are grid-edge heights as before; the `n/2` ridge cells at 100 have 8–13 of 30 refutations censored at 120 s, all above the median; two `n = 100`, `m = 50` Bernoulli instances left the solve budget uncertified and enter no peak; seconds came from a machine at load 40–45."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":32,"cache_creation_input_tokens":525,"cache_read_input_tokens":310058,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":525,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":790,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7926e52b-a7c9-488a-920f-3bf6526697d2","uuid":"04c3b255-c325-4abf-8e8e-80add283b1ec","timestamp":"2026-09-28T02:40:31.044Z","request_id":"req_011CfV4g91coXHaReyiy6tD1"}
